ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain: two faces of one cylinder (or another
surface periodic in one direction) whose seams lie half a period apart
are merged (mitcad#284).

A join of two coaxial cylinders of the same radius, one on the other,
leaves two faces of one cylindrical surface, each with its own seam; the
circle between them is cut at both seams. The face merge after the
boolean removes the seams and the circle between the faces, and builds
the merged face's seam again from the removed edges
(ReconstructMissedSeam): at each vertex it takes the removed edge that
continues from the current point in the parametric space. A removed edge
that ends at the current vertex was compared by its far end: it was taken
(turned round) when that end lay more than half a period from the current
point, and dropped when it lay less than half a period away. Where the
seams lie half a period apart, the half circle between them ends exactly
half a period from where it starts, so it was taken by neither test, the
wire could not be built and the two faces stayed apart (the stored bodies
of the designs have one face there). Such an edge is now turned to start
at the current vertex first, and its own end there is compared with the
current point (and its p-curves swapped where that end lies a period
away), on a surface periodic in one direction; the case of a surface
periodic in both is unchanged.
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
@@ -911,6 +911,18 @@
     if ((aFirstVertex.IsSame(theCurVertex) || aLastVertex.IsSame(theCurVertex))
         && BRep_Tool::IsClosed(anEdge, theFrefFace))
     {
+      // On a surface periodic in one direction, the edge is turned to start
+      // at the current vertex first, so that the point compared with the
+      // current one is the edge's end at that vertex, not its far end (an
+      // edge ending at the vertex whose far end lies half a period away,
+      // the circle between two cylinders whose seams are opposite, was
+      // taken by neither test below).
+      const bool aBothPeriodic = theUperiod != 0. && theVperiod != 0.;
+      if (!aBothPeriodic && !aFirstVertex.IsSame(theCurVertex))
+      {
+        anEdge.Reverse();
+        aPC = BRep_Tool::CurveOnSurface(anEdge, theFrefFace, Param1, Param2);
+      }
       double   aParam = (anEdge.Orientation() == TopAbs_FORWARD) ? Param1 : Param2;
       gp_Pnt2d aPoint = aPC->Value(aParam);
       double   aUdiff = std::abs(aPoint.X() - theCurPoint.X());
@@ -918,7 +930,7 @@
       if ((theUperiod != 0. && aUdiff > theUperiod / 2)
           || (theVperiod != 0. && aVdiff > theVperiod / 2))
       {
-        if (aLastVertex.IsSame(theCurVertex) || (theUperiod != 0. && theVperiod != 0.))
+        if (aBothPeriodic)
         {
           anEdge.Reverse();
         }
